              %li
                %a{:href => "#example"} Example
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\omega)
            one may consider the restriction of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+symplectic+group"} affine symplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ASp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ASp(V,\omega)
            (
            %a{:href => "#RobbinSalamon93"}> Robbin-Salamon 93, corollary 9.3
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ESp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi QuantMorph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ASp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi HamSympl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  ESp(V,\omega) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; QuantMorph(V,\omega)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  ASp(V,\omega)
                  \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                  HamSympl(V,\omega)
                  }
          %p
            Sometimes (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RobbinSalamon93"} Robbin-Salamon 93, p. 30
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ESp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ESp(V,\omega)
            is called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em extended symplectic group
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+affine+symplectic+group"} extended affine symplectic group
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#ARZ06"} ARZ 06, prop. V.1
          %p
            Notice that the further restriction to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} translation group
            over itself is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Heis
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Heis(V,\omega)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Heis
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi ESp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi QuantMorph
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi ASp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %mi HamSympl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ω
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Heis(V,\omega)
                  \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                  ESp(V,\omega) &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; QuantMorph(V,\omega)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  V
                  \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                  ASp(V,\omega)
                  \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                  HamSympl(V,\omega)
                  }
          %p
            The group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ESp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ESp(V,\omega)
            is that of those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphisms"} quantomorphisms
            which come from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonians"} Hamiltonians
            that are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quadratic+Hamiltonians"} quadratic Hamiltonians
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
            instead of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+symplectic+group"} affine symplectic group
            come from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneously+quadratic+Hamiltonians"} homogeneously quadratic Hamiltonians
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#RobbinSalamon93"} Robbin-Salamon 93, prop. 10.1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ESp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ESp
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product"} semidirect product
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+group"} metaplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mp(V,\omega)
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+group"} Heisenberg group
            (
            %a{:href => "#ARZ06"}> ARZ 06, prop. V.1
            , see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Low12"} Low 12
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ESp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Heis
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋊
                  %mi Mp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ESp(V,\omega) \simeq Heis(V,\omega) \rtimes Mp(V,\omega)
                  \\,.
          %h2#example Example
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∧
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V,\omega) = (\mathbb{R}^2, \mathbf{d}p\wedge \mathbf{d}q)
            be the 2-dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+space"} symplectic vector space
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  q,p \colon \mathbb{R}^2 \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
          %p
            for its two canonical coordinate functions (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+coordinates"} canonical coordinates
            and
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+momenta"} canonical momenta
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  i \colon \mathbb{R}^2 \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+function"} constant function
            with value 1.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi p
                  %mo .
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\{p.q\} = i
                  \\,.
          %p
            Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \colon \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}
            we may call a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+flow"} Hamiltonian flow
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flow"} flow
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+field"} vector field
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+vector+field"} Hamiltonian vector field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi H
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{H,-\}
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^2)
          %p
            Those Hamiltonians whose Hamiltonian flows are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+functions"} linear functions
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            are precisely the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homogeneously+quadratic+Hamiltonians"} homogeneously quadratic Hamiltonians
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                    %mo ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                            %mo +
                            %mi t
                            %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(t\{\tfrac{1}{2}p^2,-\})
                  \\colon
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q
                  \\\
                  p
                  }
                  \\right]
                  \\mapsto
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q +t p
                  \\\
                  p
                  }
                  \\right]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                    %mo ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                            %mo +
                            %mi t
                            %mi q
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\{\tfrac{1}{2}q^2,-\})
                  \\colon
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q
                  \\\
                  p
                  }
                  \\right]
                  \\mapsto
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q
                  \\\
                  p + t q
                  }
                  \\right]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi q
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                    %mo ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mi t
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mi t
                            %mi p
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(t \{q p,-\})
                  \\colon
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q
                  \\\
                  p
                  }
                  \\right]
                  \\mapsto
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  e^t q
                  \\\
                  e^{-t} p
                  }
                  \\right]
          %p
            The general element of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+group"} metaplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi q
                  %mo ∧
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mp(\mathbb{R}^2,\mathbf{d}q \wedge \mathbf{d}p)
            is hence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 2
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 3
                  %mi q
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(t_1 \tfrac{1}{2}p^2 + t_2 \tfrac{1}{2}q^2 + t_3 q p)
          %p
            By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiating
            this by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = 0
            we obtain a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔰𝔭
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sp}(V,\omega)
            of, both, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sp(V,\omega)
            as well as its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+group"} metaplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mp(V,\omega)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                    %mo ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                    %mo ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  0 &amp; 0
                  \\\
                  1 &amp; 0
                  }
                  \\right]
                  \\,,
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  0 &amp; 1
                  \\\
                  0 &amp; 0
                  }
                  \\right]
                  \\,,
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  1 &amp; 0
                  \\\
                  0 &amp; -1
                  }
                  \\right]
          %p The Hamiltonians that generate translations are precisely the homogeneously linear Hamiltonians:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                    %mo ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                            %mo +
                            %mi t
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(t\{p,-\})
                  \\colon
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q
                  \\\
                  p
                  }
                  \\right]
                  \\mapsto
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q + t
                  \\\
                  p
                  }
                  \\right]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                    %mo ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi p
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(t\{q,-\})
                  \\colon
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q
                  \\\
                  p
                  }
                  \\right]
                  \\mapsto
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  q
                  \\\
                  p - t
                  }
                  \\right]
          %p
            This is the key point where the extension appears: While these two linear translation operations themselves (i.e. the underlying
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectomorphisms"} symplectomorphisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+algebra"} Heisenberg algebra
            extension of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+group"} translation group
          %p
            The general element of the extended affine symplectic group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ESp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi q
                  %mo ∧
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi d
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ESp(\mathbb{R}^2, \mathbf{d}q \wedge \mathbf{d}p)
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 1
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 2
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 3
                  %mi q
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 4
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 5
                  %mi q
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mn 6
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(t_1 \tfrac{1}{2}p^2 + t_2 \tfrac{1}{2}q^2 + t_3 q p + t_4 p + t_5 q + t_6 i)
                  \\,.
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#RobbinSalamon93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joel+Robbin"}> Joel Robbin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dietmar+Salamon"} Dietmar Salamon
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Feynman path integrals on phase space and the metaplectic representation
                %strong 221
                (1996), no. 2, 307–-335, (
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=98f:58051"}> MR98f:58051
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/BF02622118"} doi
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/RobbinSalamonMetaplectic.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dietmar+Salamon"} Dietmar Salamon
                (ed.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Symplectic Geometry
            %li#ARZ06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Albeverio"}> Sergio Albeverio
                , J. Rezende and J.-C. Zambrini,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Probability and Quantum Symmetries. II. The Theorem of Noether in quantum mechanics
                = succeed ")" do
